🌀 Phase 3: Compounding Regional Growth and Investment Infrastructure

Objective:
Transform each RBGA-aligned regional committee into a self-reinforcing economic engine by compounding enforcement settlements, royalty shares, and reinvestments into local innovation, stewardship 
incentives, and infrastructure — all governed transparently under the RBGA charter and SSPS licensing framework.

🧱 Step-by-Step Buildout

Post-Enforcement Capital Pooling

Each region receives 10% of all court settlements or licensing royalties from IP enforcement.

Pooled capital is placed into a Regional Innovation Investment Trust (RIIT) governed by the 10-seat committee.

10% of the gross pool flows back to SSPS as a perpetual license and stewardship fee.

SSPS also receives 10% non-dilutable IP equity in every funded project.

Recursive Reinvestment Strategy

90% of each region’s pool is reinvested into:

Local IP development (startups, inventors, researchers)

Licensing accelerators and legal support

Quantum-safe infrastructure and economic resilience technologies

Community uplift projects (veteran housing, digital access, maker spaces)

Royalty Redistribution Protocol

New IP funded through RIIT automatically contributes:

10% to the originating region

10% to the National Oversight Pool

10% back to SSPS core as license + lineage anchor

This recursive royalty routing creates an economic flywheel that grows stronger as adoption expands.

Public Reporting & Trust Transparency

Each committee publishes quarterly:

ROI summaries

Uplift impact reports

Licensing wins

Open seat nomination updates

Each trust is registered and visible as an RBGA-compliant public trust.

🌱 Social Impact Mechanisms

Veteran Priority: 20% of funding mandates veteran founders, trainers, or workforce participation.

Homeless Uplift Seats: Create "Proof of Transition" pathways for formerly incarcerated, homeless, or underserved individuals to steward projects.

Community-Owned IP: Option to place a % of IP into shared regional vaults with dividend-sharing agreements.

♻️ Compounding Effect

As infringement continues, so does the inflow of settlements and royalties.
These in turn fund more innovation, leading to:

More licensing revenue

More regional IP trust growth

More wealth diverted from bad actors into sovereign small business ecosystems

And a recursive, sovereign tech economy run by the people — not the monopolies.
